$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"HolyC"$$FG$
$FG,4$$TX+CX,"(desecrated)"$$FG$

This scripture has been desecrated.  The language formerly known as HolyC is now $LK,"Unholy C",A="FI:::/Doc/UnholyC.DD"$.  Nothing was taken away: every HolyC program still compiles, and the complete language reference lives on in $LK,"::/Doc/UnholyC.DD"$, next to the backmasked keywords.

A few relics are kept on this page, because old links still point at them.

$FG,5$Relic: DemoHolyC$FG$

HolyC next to C.  A char const all alone is sent to $LK,"PutChars",A="MN:PutChars"$().  A string with or without args is sent to $LK,"Print",A="MN:Print"$().  An empty string literal signals a variable fmt_str follows.

$ID,2$$FG,2$void DemoC(char drv,char *fmt,char *name,int age)
{
  printf("Hello World!\n");
  printf("%s age %d\n",name,age);
  printf(fmt,name,age);
  putchar(drv);
  putchar('*');
}

U0 DemoHolyC(U8 drv,U8 *fmt,U8 *name,I64 age)
{
  "Hello World!\n";
  "%s age %d\n",name,age;
  "" fmt,name,age;
  '' drv;
  '*';
}
$FG$$ID,-2$
The same thing, played backwards, is $FG,2$DemoUnholyC$FG$ in $LK,"Unholy C",A="FF:::/Doc/UnholyC.DD,DemoUnholyC"$.

$FG,5$Relic: The Tablet of Precedence$FG$

HolyC $LK,"operator precedence",A="FF:::/Doc/UnholyC.DD,operator precedence"$, highest first.  Unholy C kept it unchanged:
  $FG,2$`$FG$,$FG,2$>>$FG$,$FG,2$<<$FG$
  $FG,2$*$FG$,$FG,2$/$FG$,$FG,2$%$FG$
  $FG,2$&$FG$
  $FG,2$^$FG$
  $FG,2$|$FG$
  $FG,2$+$FG$,$FG,2$-$FG$
  $FG,2$<$FG$,$FG,2$>$FG$,$FG,2$<=$FG$,$FG,2$>=$FG$
  $FG,2$==$FG$,$FG,2$!=$FG$
  $FG,2$&&$FG$
  $FG,2$^^$FG$
  $FG,2$||$FG$
  $FG,2$=$FG$,$FG,2$<<=$FG$,$FG,2$>>=$FG$,$FG,2$*=$FG$,$FG,2$/=$FG$,$FG,2$&=$FG$,$FG,2$|=$FG$,$FG,2$^=$FG$,$FG,2$+=$FG$,$FG,2$-=$FG$

